layed in an exhibition</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t3-l-q21\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>a book about a botanic garden</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t3-l-q21\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>carpets he saw on holiday</span></div></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">22</strong><span>Jim eventually decided to do a practical investigation which involved</span></span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t3-l-q22\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>using a range of dyes with different fibres.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t3-l-q22\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>applying different dyes to one type of fibre.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t3-l-q22\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>testing one dye and a range of fibres.</span></div></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">23</strong><span>When doing his experiments, Jim was surprised by</span></span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t3-l-q23\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>how much natural material was needed to make the dye.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t3-l-q23\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>the fact that dyes were widely available on the internet.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t3-l-q23\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>the time that he had to leave the fabric in the dye.</span></div></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">24</strong><span>What problem did Jim have with using tartrazine as a fabric dye?</span></span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t3-l-q24\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>It caused a slight allergic reaction.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t3-l-q24\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>It was not a permanent dye on cotton.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t3-l-q24\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>It was ineffective when used on nylon.</span></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":4},{"id":"en-c13-t3-l-g3-1","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"matching_features","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 25-30","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><p>What problem is identified with each of the following natural dyes?</p><p><em>Choose&nbsp;<strong>SIX</strong>&nbsp;answers from the box and write the correct letter,&nbsp;<strong>A-H</strong>, next to Questions</em></p><p><strong>Problems</strong></p><p><strong>Natural</strong>&nbsp;<strong>dyes</strong></p></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"matching-dnd-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>turmeric</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">25</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t3-l-q25\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>beetroot</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">26</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t3-l-q26\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>Tyrian purple</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">27</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t3-l-q27\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>logwood</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">28</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t3-l-q28\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>cochineal</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">29</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t3-l-q29\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>metal oxide</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">30</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t3-l-q30\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div></div><div class=\"options-dnd-panel dnd-panel dnd-panel--matching\"><div class=\"dnd-panel-instruction\">Drag and drop an option to fill in each blank.</div><div class=\"dnd-cards-container\"><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"A\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">A.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">It is expensive.</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"B\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">B.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">The colour is too strong.</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"C\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">C.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">The colour is not long-lasting.</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"D\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">D.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">It is very poisonous.</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"E\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">E.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">It can damage the fabric.</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"F\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">F.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">The colour may be unexpected.</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"G\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">G.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">It is unsuitable for some fabrics.</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"H\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">H.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">It is not generally available</span></div></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":6}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/cambridge-ielts-13-academic-listening-3-audio-3.mp3"],"order_index":3},{"id":"en-c13-t3-l-p4","title":"Part 4","part_number":4,"passage_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/12447-cambridge-ielts-13-academic-listening-3-audio-4.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-c13-t3-l-g4-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 31-40","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p>Complete the notes below.</p><p>Write&nbsp;<strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong>&nbsp;for each answer.</p><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong><strong>The sleepy lizard (<em>tiliqua rugosa</em>)</strong></strong></p><p><strong>Description</strong></p><ul><li>They are common in Western and South Australia</li><li>They are brown, but recognisable by their blue <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">31</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t3-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li><li>They are relatively large</li><li>Their diet consists mainly of <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">32</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t3-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li><li>Their main predators are large birds and <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t3-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li></ul><p><strong>Navigation study</strong></p><ul><li>One study found that lizards can use the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t3-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;to help them navigate</li></ul><p><strong>Observations in the wild</strong></p><ul><li>Observations show that these lizards keep the same <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t3-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;for several years</li></ul><p><strong>What people want</strong></p><ul><li>Possible reasons:</li></ul><p>–&nbsp; to improve the survival of their young</p><p>(but little <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t3-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;has been noted between parents and children)</p><p>–&nbsp; to provide <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t3-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;for female lizards</p><p><strong>Tracking study</strong></p><p>–&nbsp; A study was carried out using GPS systems attached to the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t3-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;of the lizards</p><p>–&nbsp; This provided information on the lizards’ location and even the number of <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t3-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;taken</p><p>–&nbsp; It appeared that the lizards were trying to avoid one another</p><p>–&nbsp; This may be in order to reduce chances of <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t3-l-q40\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></p></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":10}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/cambridge-ielts-13-academic-listening-3-audio-4.mp3"],"order_index":4}],"questions":[{"id":"en-c13-t3-l-q1","part_id":"en-c13-t3-l-p1","group_id":"en-c13-t3-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"850","correct_answer_variants":["850"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[1],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_12425_1","order_index":1,"points":1},{"id":"en-c13-t3-l-q2","part_id":"en-c13-t3-l-p1","group_id":"en-c13-t3-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"bike/bicycle","correct_answer_variants":["bike","bicycle"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[2],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_12425_2","order_index":2,"points":1},{"id":"en-c13-t3-l-q3","part_id":"en-c13-t3-l-p1","group_id":"en-c13-t3-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"parking","correct_answer_variants":["parking"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[3],"sourceInputName":"